# Test fixture 06 — malformed `---` (wrong hyphen count).
#
# Per spec §4.1: the separator is EXACTLY three hyphens. Two hyphens
# is a Rust-style range; four+ hyphens looks like a horizontal rule.
# Neither is the settlement separator. The tokenizer must refuse.
#
# Expected: tokenize FAILS at the malformed line
#           (`-- is not a recognized form; expected --- or other token`).

in @io

grammar @test/06/malformed_separator {
  glass to @io {}
}

--

# Two hyphens — the substrate refuses.
